{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing mechanoluminescence (ML) thermal stability by engineering intrinsic lattice disorder in Sr3Gd2(Ge3O9)2:Mn2+. The researchers created a quasi-continuous trap landscape using diverse local crystal-field environments and dynamically generated defects, enabling a trap-relay process. This approach sustains stable ML across an ultrabroad temperature range (133–433 K), demonstrating potential for extreme-temperature applications without external power. The findings address the limitation of narrow thermal windows in conventional ML materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered intrinsic lattice disorder in Sr3G:Gd2(Ge3O9)2:Mn2+ enables a quasi-continuous trap landscape",
    "Trap-relay process sustains stable mechanoluminescence across 133–433 K",
    "Demonstrated human-machine interaction under simulated extreme-temperature conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes intrinsic lattice disorder as a general strategy to broaden the thermal operating window of mechanoluminescent materials, advancing the design of thermally robust, energy-storing luminescent systems for extreme environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether Modified Fangji Huangqi Decoction (MFHD) alleviates IgA nephropathy (IgAN) through gut microbiota modulation. Using UPLC-MS/MS, metagenomics, and immune profiling in IgAN mice, MFHD reduced urinary protein and renal damage while increasing gut microbiota diversity. It enriched Fusicatenibacter saccharivorans, which restored Th17/Treg balance, decreased IgA+ plasma cells, and improved intestinal barrier function via occludin/ZO-1 upregulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MFHD reduces urinary protein and renal pathology in IgAN mice",
    "MFHD enriches Fusicatenibacter saccharivorans to rebalance Th17/Treg immune cells",
    "Fusicatenibacter saccharivorans suppresses IgA+ plasma cell differentiation and enhances intestinal barrier integrity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies a specific gut bacterium that mediates MFHD's renoprotective effects in IgAN, providing mechanistic insights into microbiota-immune axis modulation for this kidney disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window prevents amplification. Mechanistically, HFD recruits neutrophils that express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cells. After recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. These findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states can durably reprogram immune responses when coinciding with tissue inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute inflammation to chronic obesity levels in lean mice",
    "HFD outside this temporal window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window prevents inflammatory amplification",
    "Neutrophil-mediated Nlrp3-Il1b signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells after recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a dietary window mechanism where transient metabolic states can durably reprogram immune memory during tissue inflammation, providing insights into how short-lived physiological changes impact long-term immune responses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how dynamic covalent bonds in polymer networks influence molecular transport using super-resolution microscopy. The research compared unhydrated networks with and without thiol-thioester dynamic covalent chemistry (DCC), adding catalysts to observe effects on probe diffusion. Results showed that catalyst additives significantly increased mobile fraction and produced more fluid-like diffusivity without macroscopic plasticization. The findings indicate that small additive concentrations can enhance transport by restructuring heterogeneous networks, potentially aiding separation and controlled-release applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Catalyst additives increased mobile fraction and diffusivity in DCC networks",
    "Enhanced transport occurred without macroscopic plasticization",
    "Restructuring of heterogeneous networks, not local bond exchange, drove transport improvements"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that strategic additive incorporation can fluidize molecular transport in covalent adaptable networks through network restructuring, providing insights for stimuli-responsive materials design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the role of regulatory T cell (Treg)-associated genes in colorectal cancer (CRC) using single-cell RNA sequencing and multi-omics approaches. Researchers identified MED10 as a critical Treg-related gene, with high expression correlating with shortened survival. Functional assays demonstrated MED10 knockdown impaired CRC cell proliferation, migration, and Wnt/β-catenin signaling, while in vivo models showed reduced tumor growth and enhanced Treg infiltration following MED10 silencing. These findings suggest MED10's role in CRC progression and immunosuppression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MED10 expression correlates with shortened survival in colorectal cancer",
    "MED10 knockdown impairs CRC cell proliferation, migration, and Wnt/β-catenin signaling",
    "MED10 silencing reduces tumor growth and enhances effector T-cell activity in vivo"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study identifies MED10 as a key regulator in colorectal cancer immune evasion, linking Treg activity to Wnt/β-catenin signaling and immunosuppressive microenvironment remodeling."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how crystalline packing in semicrystalline polymers affects liquid wettability and droplet mobility. By incorporating poly(octadecyl acrylate) into a porous polymer coating, researchers controlled crystallization through melting and cooling pathways. The approach generated reversible hydrophilic, hydrophobic, and amphiphobic states with surface tensions of 22-72 mN m-1, enabling programmable droplet spreading, pinning, and low-friction transport without post-synthetic modifications or external stimuli.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reversible switching between hydrophilic (θW ∼ 85°), hydrophobic (θW ∼ 104°), and amphiphobic slippery states via crystalline packing control",
    "Programmable droplet spreading, pinning, and low-friction transport across surface tensions of 22-72 mN m-1",
    "Reconfigurable wettability patterns enabling guided liquid transport through spatially selective wetting"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a crystallinity-driven mechanism for dynamically tuning liquid wettability and mobility, providing a versatile platform for applications requiring reversible, stimulus-free control of liquid behavior on solid surfaces."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered SIM0278, an IL-2 mutein fused to a human Fc fragment, to enhance regulatory T cell (Treg) selectivity while minimizing conventional T cell activation. The variant demonstrated reduced binding to IL-2Rβγ, preferential STAT5 activation in Tregs, and robust therapeutic efficacy across multiple autoimmune disease models and cynomolgus monkeys. It expanded Tregs and reduced inflammation, autoantibodies, and mortality in preclinical models without significant off-target effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SIM0278 selectively expands Tregs over conventional T cells by attenuating IL-2Rβγ binding",
    "The mutein showed dose-dependent therapeutic effects in multiple autoimmune disease models",
    "SIM0278 exhibited prolonged half-life and sustained Treg expansion in cynomolgus monkeys"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study provides a proof-of-concept for engineering IL-2 variants with enhanced Treg selectivity and prolonged half-life, advancing targeted immunomodulation for autoimmune disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates flexible, high-speed organic photodiode arrays for near-infrared imaging. Researchers developed pseudo-planar heterojunction (PPHJ) OPD arrays with tailored vertical phase separation and donor-acceptor interfaces, achieving high responsivity (0.6 A/W at .868 μm), low dark current (1.5 × 10^-8 A/cm² at -1 V), and fast response (480 ns). The integrated dynamic organic photonics imaging system (DOIS) enabled dynamic imaging with enhanced resolution via pixel-shifting in CNN algorithms. The work addresses key constraints in flexible organic imaging systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PPHJ OPD arrays achieved high responsivity (0.6 A/W at 868 nm)",
    "Low dark current (1.5 × 10^-8 A/cm² at -1 V) and fast response (480 ns)",
    "Pixel-shifting in CNN algorithms improved dynamic imaging resolution"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances organic photodetector technology for flexible, low-noise near-infrared imaging by integrating optimized material design with machine learning-enhanced imaging systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This randomized controlled trial protocol evaluates Jin's three-needle acupuncture for functional recovery in ischemic stroke patients. The study compares this therapy against sham acupuncture, measuring clinical outcomes via NIHSS, MBI, and mRS scores, alongside peripheral immune markers and rs-fMRI functional connectivity changes. The protocol aims to establish links between neuroimmune mechanisms and clinical improvement during stroke recovery.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Assessment of clinical efficacy using NIHSS, MBI, and mRS scores",
    "Measurement of peripheral immune markers including regulatory T cell proportion and PAI-1 levels",
    "Exploration of rs-fMRI functional connectivity changes associated with clinical outcomes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This protocol provides a methodological framework for investigating neuroimmune mechanisms underlying acupuncture-induced functional recovery in ischemic stroke, advancing understanding of multimodal therapeutic interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates optimizing aluminum current collectors for sodium metal batteries using a tailored copper layer with nickel-yttrium diatomic catalyst (NiY-DAC). The approach involves magnetron sputtering and heat treatment to create ultra-long helical carbon nanofiber (CNF) 3D-networks on Al. Results show efficient sodium deposition, dendrite suppression, and high electrochemical stability with 99.49% coulombic efficiency over 3000 hours and stable cycling in full cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NiY-DAC confined in a 20 nm copper layer enables ultra-long helical CNF 3D-networks on Al current collectors",
    "The modified collector achieves 99.49% coulombic efficiency over 3000 hours at 1.0 mA cm-2",
    "Full cells demonstrate stable cycling for 1500 cycles at 10 C with low overpotential (3.1 mV)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a diatomic catalyst confinement strategy for designing high-conductivity current collectors that enhance sodium deposition kinetics and suppress dendrite formation in sodium metal batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used single-cell RNA sequencing to characterize immune cell heterogeneity and key gene expression in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC). It identified distinct transcriptional patterns across immune subpopulations, including elevated expression of specific genes in regulatory T cells and natural killer T cells. The SPP1 signaling pathway was computationally inferred as a potential mediator of immune cell communication. Pseudotime analysis revealed dynamic transcriptional states, suggesting temporal changes in gene expression within the tumor microenvironment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Distinct transcriptional patterns in immune cell subpop: regulatory T cells and natural killer T cells showed elevated expression of specific genes",
    "SPP1 signaling pathway identified as a potential mediator of immune cell communication in ESCC",
    "Pseudotime analysis revealed dynamic transcriptional state changes indicating temporal gene expression variation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides single-cell resolution insights into immune cell heterogeneity and key signaling pathways in esophageal squamous cell carcinoma, advancing understanding of tumor microenvironment dynamics for potential immunotherapeutic targeting."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates creating highly reflective optical materials using only biopolymers. Researchers developed a dense-porous periodic architecture with alternating dense pectin layers and porous cellulose nanofiber layers. The approach leveraged differences in skeletal rigidity between pectin and cellulose nanofibers. The resulting films achieved reflectivities exceeding 97% in visible light and 95% in near-infrared, representing a significant advancement for sustainable photonics with potential applications in thermal management.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Achieved reflectivities exceeding 97% in visible light and 95% in near-infrared using polysaccharide-based multilayers",
    "Utilized alternating dense pectin and porous cellulose nanofiber layers to create the periodic architecture",
    "Demonstrated scalable fabrication with potential for thermal management applications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel design principle for highly reflective, biodegradable photonic materials using biopolymers, advancing sustainable photonics by overcoming refractive index limitations inherent to biopolymers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates LDHA's role in tumor metabolic reprogramming, focusing on its spatial heterogeneity and correlation with tumor malignancy. Using biochemical and immunohistochemical analyses, it demonstrates LDHA's elevated expression at invasive tumor edges, driving lactate production that fuels glycolysis, suppresses immune responses, and promotes immunosuppressive stromal cell functions. The findings highlight LD. HA's contribution to tumor progression and potential therapeutic targeting.",
  "key_findings": [
    "LDHA expression is significantly higher at invasive tumor edges compared to less invasive regions",
    "Lactate produced by LDHA drives immunosuppression by inhibiting T cell function and promoting M2 macrophage polarization",
    "LDHA-mediated metabolic reprogramming correlates with tumor malignancy and offers targets for therapeutic intervention"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes LDHA as a central regulator of tumor metabolic symbiosis and immunosuppression, providing a mechanistic basis for targeting lactate metabolism to overcome therapeutic resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates photonic liquid crystal networks capable of decoupling structural color and mechanical motion responses. The material remains colorless when dry but, upon water absorption, exhibits vivid coloration and programmable 3D deformation. Ethanol selectively triggers color without motion, while heat induces motion without color. This stimulus-selective control enables independent manipulation of optical and mechanical outputs for applications in soft robotics, adaptive camouflage, and smart displays.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Photonic liquid crystal networks decouple structural color and mechanical motion responses",
    "Water absorption triggers simultaneous vivid coloration and programmable 3D deformation",
    "Ethanol selectively activates color without motion, while heat induces motion without color"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a stimulus-selective mechanism for independently controlling optical and mechanical outputs in a single material, advancing multi-responsive soft matter systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examined BMDC-derived exosomes' efficacy in alleviating ovariectomy-induced depression in rats. Using an intravenous exosome treatment regimen, researchers observed reduced neuronal apoptosis, normalized microglial activation, and restored T-cell homeostasis. The exosomes suppressed NF-κB-mediated neuroinflammation, shifting microglia from pro-inflammatory M1 to anti-inflammatory M2 phenotypes. These findings suggest exosomes may offer a targeted immunomodulatory approach for post-menopausal depression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BMDC-derived exosomes suppressed NF-κB activation and reduced pro-inflammatory cytokines in ovariectomized rats",
    "Exosomes restored T-cell homeostasis by normalizing CD4, CD8, and regulatory T-cell populations",
    "Exosome treatment shifted microglial phenotype from M1 to M2, alleviating depression symptoms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies BMDC-derived exosomes as a potential immunomodulatory mechanism for mitigating neuroinflammation-driven depression in post-menopausal models."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines phase engineering strategies for two-dimensional topological materials (2D TMs), covering growth techniques, phase modulation methods, and device applications. It highlights the progression from fundamental physics to practical implementations, emphasizing challenges in scaling up synthesis and integrating topological phases into functional electronics. The study underscores the critical role of material fabrication in realizing 2D TMs' potential for quantum computing and advanced electronics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Systematic discussion of growth methods for 2D topological materials",
    "Review of phase modulation techniques enabling topological state engineering",
    "Identification of key barriers in transitioning 2D TMs from research to device applications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a comprehensive framework for advancing two-dimensional topological materials from synthesis to functional devices, addressing critical gaps in phase engineering for quantum computing applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how sensory-neuroimmune interactions influence the immune microenvironment in cold head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) tumors. Using orthotopic HNSCC models, researchers found sensory hyperexcitability promotes tumor growth, and interrupting sensory signaling reduced tumor progression. Genetic deletion of calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) enhanced radioimmunotherapy efficacy by decreasing regulatory T cell infiltration and immunosuppressive activity. High-dose psilocybin temporarily suppressed tumor growth by inhibiting CGRP and boosting antitumor immunity, with effects partially reversed by clopidogrel and linked to serotonin changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Sensory hyperexcitability in HNSCC models drives tumor growth and is reversible via sensory signaling interruption",
    "CGRP genetic knockout with radioimmunotherapy eradicated tumors by reducing regulatory T cell infiltration",
    "High-dose psilocybin transiently inhibits tumor growth through CGRP suppression and enhanced antitumor immunity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies neurogenic inflammation as a modifiable factor in cold tumors, providing a mechanistic basis for targeting sensory-neuroimmune crosstalk to overcome immunosuppression in solid tumors."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates planar focusing of anisotropic plasmon polaritons using a MoOCl2/Au heterostructure. The researchers converted surface plasmon polaras (SPPs) into surface plasmon hyperbolic polaritons (SPHPs) by integrating an Au metastructure with MoOCl2, a hyperbolic material. They optimized MoOCl2 thickness to enhance propagation distance and field compression. Using SNOM, they achieved a focal length of 2.5λ and a focal spot FWHM of λ/5 at 633 nm, with threefold energy enhancement. This visible-frequency system enables long-distance nanoscale focusing for applications in noncontact probing, integrated photonics, and optical interconnects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Conversion of surface plasmon polaritons to surface plasmon hyperbolic polaritons in MoOCl2/Au heterostructure",
    "Optimized MoOCl2 thickness achieved focal length of 2.5λ and focal spot FWHM of λ/5 at 633 nm",
    "Threefold energy enhancement in the focusing process"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates visible-frequency planar focusing of anisotropic plasmon polaritons with extended focal length, advancing hyperbolic polariton applications in nanoscale optical manipulation beyond mid-infrared and terahertz regimes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether CD4+ T cell anergy in transplantation tolerance requires continuous regulatory T cell (Treg)-dependent control of IL-2 availability. Using murine models of cardiac allograft tolerance and repeated alloantigen exposure, researchers found that anti-CD154-induced Tconv anergy depends on Tregs to sustain IL-2 limitation. Treg depletion reinvigorated anergic Tconvs by increasing IL-2 availability, indicating anergy maintenance requires ongoing Treg-mediated IL-2 regulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Anti-CD154-mediated Tconv anergy requires continuous Treg-dependent control of IL-2 availability for maintenance",
    "Treg depletion reinvigorated previously anergic Tconvs by increasing IL-2 availability",
    "Exogenous IL-2 can partially restore Tconv function by bypassing Treg-mediated IL-2 regulation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that Treg-mediated IL-2 limitation is essential for sustaining CD4+ T cell anergy in transplantation tolerance, revealing a critical mechanism for long-term immune quiescence without cell-intrinsic anergy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates surface passivation strategies for InSb colloidal quantum dots to enhance short-wave infrared photodetection. Using density functional theory and facet-specific exchange, researchers identified two distinct oxide-derived trap pathways on polar {111} facets. They developed orthogonal passivation that simultaneously targets In- and Sb-terminated facets, reducing hole-trap density by fivefold and improving hole mobility sixfold. The resulting photodetectors achieved 50% external quantum efficiency at 1390 nm with high stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Orthogonal passivation of In- and Sb-terminated {111} facets eliminates two distinct oxide-derived trap pathways",
    "Fivefold reduction in hole-trap density and sixfold improvement in hole mobility compared to thiol-only controls",
    "50% external quantum efficiency at 1390 nm with 580 ns fall time and 95% photocurrent retention after 100 hours"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a facet-specific passivation strategy that overcomes surface trap limitations in InSb quantum dots, enabling high-performance short-wave infrared photodetectors without heavy metals."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines immune dysregulation in type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM), highlighting metaflammation across multiple tissues. It details how various leukocyte lineages contribute to metabolic dysfunction, including adipose macrophages, dendritic cells, and T cells. The study evaluates ten natural products targeting key immune pathways like NF-κB and NLRP3 inflammasome. It emphasizes translation challenges, such as pharmacokinetics and biomarker validation, without claiming specific therapeutic efficacy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Metaflammation in T2DM involves multiple immune cell types across metabolic tissues",
    "Ten natural products target specific immune pathways implicated in T2DM pathogenesis",
    "Significant barriers exist for translating natural products into clinical applications due to pharmacokinetics and biomarker limitations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review clarifies the immunological mechanisms underlying T2DM and identifies natural products as potential modulators of immune-mediated metabolic dysfunction, though clinical translation requires addressing pharmacokinetic and biomarker challenges."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates dislocation-mediated heat transport in 5°SrTiO3 low-angle grain boundaries using operando scanning transmission electron microscopy with electron energy-loss spectroscopy thermometry. The approach combines atomic-resolution imaging, vibrational spectroscopy, and nonequilibrium molecular dynamics to map thermal resistance across dislocation arrays. Results show an effective thermal conductance of ∼35.4 MW m-2 K-1, corresponding to a Kapitza length of ∼339 nm. Dislocation cores act as sharp thermal bottlenecks over 2.14-5.17 nm, while inter-core regions exhibit weaker modulation over 8.34-11.57 nm. The findings reveal how atomic-scale core reconstruction creates nanoscale thermal resistance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dislocation cores function as sharp thermal bottlenecks over 2.14-5.17 nm",
    "Inter-core regions show weaker thermal modulation over 8.34-11.57 nm",
    "Atomic-scale core reconstruction generates nanoscale localized thermal resistance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides quantitative descriptors for defect-structure-guided thermal design by elucidating the nanoscale mechanisms of dislocation-mediated thermal resistance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the design requirements for chimeric antigen receptor regulatory T cells (CAR-Tregs) targeting autoimmunity. It addresses how autoimmune lesions' heterogeneity, dynamic nature, and inflammatory challenges necessitate tailored engineering strategies. The research emphasizes matching CAR-Treg recognition, function, stability, and persistence to tissue-specific biological constraints rather than maximizing suppressive potency. Key findings include the critical role of target architecture, context-dependent regulatory outputs, and maintaining Treg identity under inflammatory conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Target selection must account for antigen presentation, accessibility, tissue distribution, and productive CAR engagement.",
    "Functional programming requires inducible and locally restricted regulatory outputs beyond constitutive suppression.",
    "Durable Treg activity depends on maintaining identity under inflammatory stress through coordinated FOXP3 expression and receptor signaling."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that effective CAR-Tregs for autoimmunity must align with tissue-specific disease biology rather than universal suppressive capacity, advancing precision immunotherapy design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses periodontitis treatment limitations by engineering a microenvironment-responsive photodynamic therapy (PDT) strategy. The approach utilizes Bi2O2CO3 nanosheet-assembled microspheres that scavenge pathological hydrogen sulfide (H2S) in periodontal pockets, triggering in situ formation of Bi2O2CO3@Bi2S3 heterojunctions. This H2S-triggered conversion neutralizes pro-inflammatory H2S and enhances photocatalytic activity, leading to efficient eradication of periodontopathogens like Porphyromonas gingivalis through ROS-mediated oxidative stress and bacterial iron metabolism disruption. In vivo rat models showed reduced inflammation, bone loss, and improved tissue regeneration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "H2S scavenging by Bi2O2CO3 microspheres triggers in situ formation of Bi2O2CO3@Bi2S3 heterojunctions",
    "The heterojunction neutralizes pro-inflammatory H2S and enhances photocatalytic activity for ROS production",
    "In vivo treatment reduced inflammation, alveolar bone loss, and promoted tissue regeneration in periodontitis models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a microenvironment-adaptive photodynamic therapy strategy that converts pathological hydrogen sulfide into a therapeutic amplifier, offering a novel approach to address periodontitis through targeted immunomodulation and pathogen eradication."
}
